1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,136
Getting started.

2
00:00:01,176 --> 00:00:03,560
Set it up and give it the
one permission it needs.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,395
Open Gesture Volume.

4
00:00:05,435 --> 00:00:06,926
The first time you open it,

5
00:00:06,966 --> 00:00:10,160
a short tour shows how the
bar works, one page at a time.

6
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:11,264
Pick a style.

7
00:00:11,304 --> 00:00:14,358
Simple puts a round button
on the edge for volume.

8
00:00:14,398 --> 00:00:18,875
Advanced adds the Dock, the Quick
slider, the Deck and a long-press menu.

9
00:00:18,915 --> 00:00:20,360
You can switch any time.

10
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:21,835
Learn the moves.

11
00:00:21,875 --> 00:00:25,875
The next pages play each
gesture out: swipe for volume,

12
00:00:25,915 --> 00:00:28,960
tap for the volume panel, hold to move it.

13
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:30,989
Allow the bar on screen.

14
00:00:31,029 --> 00:00:35,743
Tap Allow, switch on Allow display
over other apps, and come back.

15
00:00:35,783 --> 00:00:39,560
That one switch lets the
bar sit on top of your apps.

16
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:42,156
Notifications, if you like. Optional:

17
00:00:42,196 --> 00:00:46,809
allow notifications and the bar’s
controls wait in your notification shade,

18
00:00:46,849 --> 00:00:48,360
even with the app closed.

19
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,173
Turn on the service.

20
00:00:50,213 --> 00:00:53,350
Tap Service inactive to switch the bar on.

21
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:57,360
Go home, and the round button
is waiting on the edge.

22
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:02,710
Up next: Volume with a swipe.
